       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the usual maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Daily dose:** The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in many labels. 5,100 mg/day is well above both.\n- **Single dose:** A single dose of 1,700 mg is also far above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. A dose that high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possibilities are 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1,700 mg total per day, for example 850 mg twice daily. Please tell me the dose you intended. I'll enter it once you confirm.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical reason. I can enter it with a note, but I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
